# JRM HRMS Enterprise V3.0 Production Integration Implementation Plan

This implementation plan covers the transition of JRM HRMS Enterprise from a partially mocked state to a 100% database-backed, real-time sync system using Supabase and the Local TCP Connector.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Database Schema Provisioning**: We will write a comprehensive SQL schema file [supabase_vms_and_tenant_tables.sql](file:///f:/TEST%20LIVE%20ATTENDANCE/supabase_vms_and_tenant_tables.sql) to create `visitors`, `visitor_passes`, `visitor_logs`, `visitor_audit_logs`, `visitor_notifications`, `companies` (extended columns), and `branches` tables. The user should run this SQL script in the Supabase SQL editor.
> - **Enrollment Queue Flow**: We will connect the Enrollment Queue UI strictly to database columns, query employee details using joins, and subscribe to Supabase realtime notifications for live status updates.
> - **Visitor Management**: We will fully wire VMS to the database tables, removing all in-memory mock datasets and demo stats, and implementing complete CRUD operations.
> - **Company & Branch Management**: Hardcoded company settings and branch arrays will be replaced with queries to database tables (`companies`, `branches`).
> - **Device Connector & TCP Live Panel**: Connect device statistics and connection health state to live database heartbeat logs and real-time events.

